        {
          "question": "e-4439",
          "field": null,
          "attribute": "question/worked-solution",
          "value": "The minor of $b_{21} = 3$ (second row, first column) is the determinant of the remaining entries when the column and row containing $3$ are removed: \n\n$$\n[\\begin{aligned}\u2217 & 1 & 5 \\\\ 3 & \u2217 & \u2217 \\\\ \u2217 & 7 & 2\\end{aligned}]\n$$\n\nSo, the minor of $b_{21}=3$ is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}det[\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}] & =|\\begin{aligned}1 & 5 \\\\ 7 & 2\\end{aligned}| \\\\  & =1\\cdot 2-5\\cdot 7 \\\\  & =2-35 \\\\  & =-33.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
          "category": "ma_capture",
          "file": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/13973600/example-4439.json",
          "file_sha256": "52f40ccd834aaab7ac53f555879411bf4897dc5b68d572af815dc32e7284b121"
